# IdentityForge backend build context (IF-V4-02, v5).
#
# The backend Dockerfile installs the pinned requirements and copies
# src/ only. Without this file, a build context could carry the local
# virtualenv, the runtime evidence database (backend/data/*.db),
# caches, test artefacts and archives into the image.
#
# Kept in the context (the images need them): src/**, tests/** (the
# test profile mounts tests read-only, but they must stay available
# to any image that copies them), pyproject.toml,
# requirements-freeze.txt, requirements.txt, pytest.ini, Dockerfile,
# docker/prepare-data-volume.py (IF-V8-42 one-shot volume prep,
# copied into the backend image for the backend-data-prep service).
.venv/
venv/
data/
*.db
*.sqlite*
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/
test-results/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.git/
*.log
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*Zone.Identifier
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
